{%- comment -%}
  Font preloads.

  The @font-face rules that used to live here were an exact duplicate of the ones at the
  top of assets/bundle.theme.css - same five families, same five files, same
  font-display: swap. The only difference was the URL: this file used `asset_url`, which
  appends ?v=<hash>, while the bundle uses a relative url(). Two URLs for one file meant
  the browser fetched walsheim-regular.static.woff2 twice on every page load. The bundle
  now owns the declarations.

  Preloads are stripped of the ?v= query for the same reason: a preload only satisfies a
  later request when the URL matches exactly, and the bundle asks for the unversioned
  path. `asset_url | split: '?' | first` produces the identical URL.

  Only the two families used for body copy and headings are preloaded. walsheim-medium,
  walsheim-black and GTWalsheimPro-Regular are used by a few dozen elements each, load
  fine on demand with font-display: swap, and were previously competing with the LCP
  image for bandwidth - five preloads is roughly 205 KB on the critical path.

  ponytail: the right end state is one family with four font-weight descriptors instead
  of five family names, but `font-walsheim-bold` and friends are Tailwind classes used
  across ~1,300 elements in the theme. That rename is a P1 job, not a font-loading fix.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign font_regular = 'walsheim-regular.static.woff2' | asset_url | split: '?' | first -%}
{%- assign font_bold = 'walsheim-bold.static.woff2' | asset_url | split: '?' | first -%}

<link rel="preload" href="{{ font_regular }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous">
<link rel="preload" href="{{ font_bold }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous">
